### Requests for the IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client.
### Start the stack first: docker compose up -d, then ./mvnw -pl agent-app spring-boot:test-run

@keycloak = http://localhost:8180
@agent = http://localhost:8080

### Token as operator (olena)
# @name tokenOlena
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/workflow/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=workflow-web&username=olena&password=olena

> {% client.global.set("olena_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### Token as approver (max)
# @name tokenMax
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/workflow/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=workflow-web&username=max&password=max

> {% client.global.set("max_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### agent-app health (public)
GET {{agent}}/actuator/health

### agent-app without a token -> 401
GET {{agent}}/api/v1/instances

### Instances, newest first; filter by state, page from 0 (operator or approver)
GET {{agent}}/api/v1/instances?state=AWAIT_APPROVAL&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{olena_token}}

### One instance (no email body)
# @name instance
GET {{agent}}/api/v1/instances/{{instance_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{olena_token}}

### Its timeline: steps, model and tool calls, mails, approvals, cost
GET {{agent}}/api/v1/instances/{{instance_id}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{olena_token}}

### A model call's full text (operator only); the id comes from a LLM_CALL event of the timeline
GET {{agent}}/api/v1/instances/{{instance_id}}/llm-calls/{{llm_call_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{olena_token}}

### Approvals waiting for a decision (approver; olena gets 403)
# @name approvals
GET {{agent}}/api/v1/approvals
Authorization: Bearer {{max_token}}

> {% if (response.body.length) client.global.set("task_id", response.body[0].id); %}

### Decided ones: status=APPROVED | REJECTED | RETRIED | ESCALATED | OPEN
GET {{agent}}/api/v1/approvals?status=APPROVED
Authorization: Bearer {{max_token}}

### One task with the facts, rates, breakdown and the model's summary (made on first view)
GET {{agent}}/api/v1/approvals/{{task_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{max_token}}

### Approve, optionally at another price (never below cost: 422); a second decision is 409
POST {{agent}}/api/v1/approvals/{{task_id}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{max_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "APPROVE", "editedPrice": 1250.00, "comment": "loyal customer"}

### Reject (comment required: 400 without it)
POST {{agent}}/api/v1/approvals/{{task_id}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{max_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "REJECT", "comment": "no capacity that week"}

### Retry from UNDERSTOOD (read the email again) or ENRICHED (price again)
POST {{agent}}/api/v1/approvals/{{task_id}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{max_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "RETRY", "retryFrom": "ENRICHED", "comment": "rates were updated"}

### Operator UI (public page; it logs in through Keycloak)
GET {{agent}}/ui/

### mock-crm-mcp health
GET http://localhost:8091/actuator/health

### mock-rates health
GET http://localhost:8092/actuator/health

### Mailpit: latest messages (inbound requests and agent replies)
GET http://localhost:8025/api/v1/messages?limit=10
